## Method attribution

The chunking rules, lexical alias tiers, initials guards and literal checks in
this crate are re-implementations, from documented behaviour, of methods in
OntoCast by GrowGraph (Alexander Belikov and contributors), Apache License 2.0,
https://github.com/growgraph/ontocast, reviewed at commit
abb8d7b8d6db1a765d4f091a7423937c2cbc5d78 (version 0.6.7). No OntoCast source
code is included. The specific upstream files consulted are named in the
rustdoc of the modules that adapt them (`normalize`, `similarity`, `chunk`).

The names-in, grounded-identifiers-out extraction contract follows SPIRES:
Caufield JH, Hegde H, Emonet V, et al. "Structured prompt interrogation and
recursive extraction of semantics (SPIRES): a method for populating knowledge
bases using zero-shot learning." Bioinformatics 40(3), 2024,
doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btae104. Its implementation, OntoGPT
(https://github.com/monarch-initiative/ontogpt), is BSD-3-Clause; no OntoGPT
code is included.

The starting confidence (0.5) and method ("inferred") of every candidate
follow the retired RDF-to-Logseq adapter in DreamLab-AI/knowledgeGraph,
authored by DreamLab AI and covered by the workspace relicensing grant
(see the repository NOTICE).

